  "problem": "The additive inverse of $-\\frac{7}{8}$ is{{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "To find the additive inverse of the number $-\\frac{7}{8}$, we change its sign by placing a minus symbol $(-)$ in front of it. So, we obtain \n\n$$\n-\\,(-\\frac{7}{8})=\\frac{7}{8}.\n$$\n\nTo check our work, we simply add the inverse to the original number. If we're correct, we should get zero.\n\n$$\n(-\\frac{7}{8})+\\frac{7}{8}=-\\frac{7}{8}+\\frac{7}{8}=0\\,✓\n$$",
